  <DocumentLink id="2dfb4ea5-4ed1-53e7-b812-17303b1246cb" target-id="SD:67a8eff1-55b7-54eb-8c4e-7061917402ac" type="Default" />
  <Item id="ffebc6f0-1ebf-5ea3-91b7-21153ccbb686" type="Heading">
    <Attribute name="TestID">
      <Value>PTO-VRP-000</Value>
    </Attribute>
    <Attribute name="Contents">
      <Value>
        <Paragraph>
          <Text bold="true" font-size="+40%">Safety validation report — PTO-ECU 200 (build P2)</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>Results per ISO 25119-4:2018, 6.5. Configuration under test: HW rev C, SW 1.4.0, parameter set V7, T6100 test machine #TM-041 and HIL rig HR-2. The Margin column is a live computed attribute (Limit − Measured) — numeric rows only; qualitative tests carry 0/0.</Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>Two first-run failures were analysed and closed: PTO-VAL-009 (fender-jog stop 234 ms &gt; 200 ms — valve pilot orifice tolerance; fixed by parameter V7 jog pre-fill) and PTO-VAL-014 (spurious DTC on 100 µs micro-cuts — input filter time constant corrected in HW rev C). Both re-ran green; regression scope: VAL-004…-007.</Paragraph>
      </Value>
    </Attribute>
    <Attribute name="Result" value="2" />
    <Attribute name="Date">
      <Value>2026-07-24</Value>
    </Attribute>
    <Attribute name="Tester">
      <Value>—</Value>
    </Attribute>
  </Item>
